---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import benchmarkData from "../../data/coefficients.json";
import {
  MOVE_BASE_COST,
  MOVE_PER_MILE,
  DIY_TYPE_MULTIPLIER,
  DEFAULT_CONTINGENCY_RATE,
  DEFAULT_RANGE_LOW,
  DEFAULT_RANGE_HIGH,
} from "../lib/calculator.js";

const money = value => new Intl.NumberFormat("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD", maximumFractionDigits: 0 }).format(value);
const bands = benchmarkData.benchmarks.uhaul_one_way_average_by_distance;
const bandLabel = (band, index) => {
  const from = index === 0 ? 1 : bands[index - 1].max_miles + 1;
  return band.max_miles === null ? `${from.toLocaleString("en-US")}+ miles` : `${from.toLocaleString("en-US")}–${band.max_miles.toLocaleString("en-US")} miles`;
};
const sources = benchmarkData.sources;
const percent = value => `${Math.round(value * 100)}%`;
---
<Layout
  title="Methodology and Sources — Relocation Cost"
  description="How the Relocation Cost calculator works: the formula, every input, the sources behind the benchmarks, when they were last reviewed, and the known limits."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-sky-600">Methodology</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">How the estimates are built</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">Relocation Cost gives planning estimates, not quotes. This page shows exactly how the numbers are produced, which parts come from published sources, and which parts are assumptions.</p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Data last reviewed: {benchmarkData.last_reviewed}</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Inputs</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li><strong>Distance:</strong> filled from the great-circle distance between the geographic centers of the two states you pick, or typed by you. It is not road mileage. Replace it with your actual driving miles when you know them.</li>
      <li><strong>Home size:</strong> studio or 1 room (×1), 2–3 rooms (×1.35), 4–5 rooms (×1.8), 6+ rooms (×2.4).</li>
      <li><strong>Move type:</strong> DIY (×{DIY_TYPE_MULTIPLIER}), rental truck with labor (×1), full-service movers (×1.65).</li>
      <li><strong>Other costs:</strong> travel, temporary housing, deposits and setup, packing and extras, added exactly as you enter them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">The formula</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-4 font-mono text-sm leading-7 text-slate-800">
      <p>diy model = {money(MOVE_BASE_COST)} + distance × ${MOVE_PER_MILE} × home size × {DIY_TYPE_MULTIPLIER}</p>
      <p>diy base = the larger of the diy model and the U-Haul average for the distance band</p>
      <p>premium = distance × ${MOVE_PER_MILE} × home size × (move type − {DIY_TYPE_MULTIPLIER}), never below zero</p>
      <p>move = diy base + premium</p>
      <p>total = (move + other costs) × {(1 + DEFAULT_CONTINGENCY_RATE).toFixed(2)}</p>
      <p>range = total × {DEFAULT_RANGE_LOW.toFixed(2)} to total × {DEFAULT_RANGE_HIGH.toFixed(2)}</p>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">The {money(MOVE_BASE_COST)} base, the ${MOVE_PER_MILE} per mile rate, the home-size and move-type multipliers, the {percent(DEFAULT_CONTINGENCY_RATE)} buffer and the {percent(DEFAULT_RANGE_LOW)}–{percent(DEFAULT_RANGE_HIGH)} range are explicit planning assumptions. They are not published market prices.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">What comes from a published source</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-700">The only market figure used in the result is the U-Haul average for one-way truck rentals by distance band. It sets a minimum for the DIY base, so no estimate falls below what a one-way truck rental costs on average for that distance.</p>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm leading-6">
        <thead class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50"><tr><th class="p-3 font-semibold">Distance band</th><th class="p-3 font-semibold">U-Haul one-way average</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody class="text-slate-700">
          {bands.map((band, index) => (
            <tr class="border-b border-slate-100 last:border-0"><td class="p-3">{bandLabel(band, index)}</td><td class="p-3">{money(band.average_usd)}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Sources</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li><a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href={sources.uhaul.url} rel="noopener">{sources.uhaul.name}</a>. Data period: {sources.uhaul.data_period}. Used for: {sources.uhaul.use}.</li>
      <li><a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href={sources.bls.url} rel="noopener">{sources.bls.name}</a>. Used for: {sources.bls.use}. Laborers and freight, stock and material movers, hand: annual mean wage {money(benchmarkData.benchmarks.bls_laborers_freight_stock_material_movers_hand_mean_annual_usd)}. This figure is shown for context and does not change any result.</li>
      <li><a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href={sources.census.url} rel="noopener">{sources.census.name}</a>. Used for: {sources.census.use}.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold">Known limits</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <li>U-Haul publishes averages for distance bands. The estimate can therefore step up when the distance crosses a band boundary, for example at 1,000 miles.</li>
      <li>U-Haul states that one-way prices depend on origin, destination, truck size, move date and inventory. A band average is not a quote for your route.</li>
      <li>The labor and service premium for rental-truck and full-service moves is an assumption, not a market price.</li>
      <li>State-center distance can differ substantially from the road distance between your actual addresses.</li>
      <li>The estimate does not include insurance, taxes, utility fees or real-estate costs unless you enter them under other costs. A cost left at $0 is left out of the total. It is not known to be free.</li>
      <li>For DIY moves, the U-Haul average often sets the minimum base, so several home sizes can show the same total. That is a rule of the model and does not mean a larger home costs the same. The model has no separate truck-size price. Rental truck + labor and full-service moves add a home-size premium, so their totals differ by size.</li>
      <li>The {percent(DEFAULT_RANGE_LOW)}–{percent(DEFAULT_RANGE_HIGH)} range is a fixed planning band. It is not a statistically validated confidence interval.</li>
      <li>The base amount, per-mile rate, home-size and move-type multipliers have not been calibrated against real quotes. Calibrating them needs a set of dated, route-specific quotes, and until then they stay unchanged.</li>
      <li>Amounts are rounded to the nearest dollar for display, so the parts can differ from the total by a dollar.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-8 leading-7 text-slate-700">Always replace these estimates with written quotes for your actual addresses, dates and inventory. Ready to try it? <a class="font-semibold text-sky-700 underline" href="/calculator/">Open the calculator</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
